description:
Error handling in handleStateEvent (lines 550-589) only checks for 'cannotCalculateChanges' error type. But JMAP allows other error types like 'serverFailure', 'invalidArguments', etc.

If Message/changes returns an error (e.g., {type: 'serverFailure'}), the code proceeds to line 558:
  messageState = result.newState;

If result.newState is undefined (error response has no newState), messageState becomes undefined. Next state event will fail checks that expect messageState to be null or a string token.

Symptoms: After a /changes error, state events may crash or silently fail.

Fix: Check if result has the expected fields before using them. Pattern should be:
  if (result.type) { // any error
    handle error
    continue;
  }
  // now safe to use result.newState, etc.
